Done. Here's a summary of the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — The markup with `@typeparam TItem`. Renders each item via `ItemTemplate` with "Move Up" / "Move Down" buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — The code-behind:
- Copies `Items` into an internal `_items` list on each parameter set (never mutates the caller's list).
- Swap logic in `MoveUp`/`MoveDown`.
- Fires `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only snapshot after each reorder.

Usage matches your example — just wire up the callback:

```csharp
private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
{
    tasks = updated.ToList();
}
```
